cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Product Experimentation and Customer Value Analytics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Musoni
    given-names: Kévine
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/KevineMusoni/Product-Analytics"
abstract: >-
  Two end-to-end analyses of questions product data scientists answer every week: an A/B test of a
  retention experiment (90,189 players) and cohort retention and customer lifetime value modelling
  (23,570 customers, BG/NBD and Gamma-Gamma models) validated on a holdout. Metrics are defined in SQL
  (DuckDB), the analysis is in Python, and the models are checked against reference results by an
  automated test suite and a mutation check. Third-party datasets are documented in DATA_DICTIONARY.md.
keywords:
  - A/B testing
  - customer lifetime value
  - retention
  - BG/NBD
  - reproducibility
  - open science
